      "worked_solution": "Since the angles $\\angle{CIF}$ and $\\angle{AJI}$ are corresponding angles, they are congruent and therefore have the same measure:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CIF & =m∠AJI \\\\ 5x+{10}^{∘} & ={110}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have an equation that we can solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{10}^{∘} & ={110}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={100}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & =\\frac{{100}^{∘}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} & ={20}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={20}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
